# Security & Privacy

## Authorization

- **Authenticate** every protected endpoint. **Authorize** every action — verify the caller owns or participates in the resource (rental party, vehicle owner, etc.).
- Use NestJS guards for auth; enforce role/participation checks in services, not only in controllers.
- **Never trust the mobile client** for state transitions, ownership, or permissions — validate server-side.

## CNIC (sensitive PII)

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Collection | During registration |
| Uniqueness | One CNIC → one account (enforce at DB + service layer) |
| MVP verification | Format/normalization only — no government API, no OCR |
| Visibility | User sees own CNIC; owner and renter see each other's CNIC **only inside their rental agreement** |
| Prohibited exposure | Public profiles, vehicle listings, discovery, ratings, URLs, logs, analytics, error messages, or API responses to unrelated users |

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — CNIC in public vehicle listing DTO
{ id, make, model, ownerCnic }

// ✅ GOOD — CNIC only in rental-agreement response for participants
{ rentalId, owner: { name, cnic }, renter: { name, cnic } }
```

## Secrets & tokens

- Store JWT/session secrets, DB URLs, and object-storage credentials in environment variables only.
- Mobile: never embed secrets in the app bundle; use secure storage for tokens (Keychain/Keystore).
- Rotate-friendly token design; short-lived access tokens where applicable.

## Data handling

- Images in object storage; MongoDB stores URLs/metadata only.
- Redact CNIC and tokens from all logs, Sentry payloads, and analytics events.
- Validate and sanitize all inputs; use parameterized queries via Prisma (never raw string concatenation).

## Future-proofing

- Keep auth module interface stable so SMS/WhatsApp OTP or stronger identity verification can be added without rewriting consumers.
